# Normalize line endings to LF in the repo and on checkout — avoids CRLF/LF churn on Windows.
# Without this, a Windows checkout gets CRLF while the repo stores LF, and `dotnet format` (which defaults to the
# host's line ending) reports violations that CI never sees — a local check that disagrees with the gate is worse
# than no local check at all.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary types — never normalize
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
